Battle screenshot: We see city buildings but no monsters in view. Camera behind Godzilla? Actually the camera seems inside/behind buildings. The objective says Godzilla vs Ghidorah, but no monsters visible. Maybe camera intro positioned 260,230,420 looking at 0,60,0; but screenshot after 6s should have snapped to player. Player at z 115, camera offset behind at yaw 0 => camera at z +? CameraRig offset yaw 0 gives z positive ~240 → camera at z 355, looking at player z 115. Buildings between (at z 129) may block. Also monsters may be obscured by fog. Screenshot has red sky (sunset storm) and buildings. No monster silhouette. Need investigate positions and camera. Could be player not spawned due to error? HUD shows 2 titans. Maybe monsters are huge but behind buildings; camera at z 355 looking north; buildings at z 129 in front; player at 115 behind building row. This is a bad spawn: player starts inside building block at z 115, x 0? Central road z=86, blocks at 129. x=0,z=115 is between road 86 and block 129, maybe on block edge; camera at 355 is behind buildings. Need choose spawn in open road/plaza with clear line.

Also city at 129 blocks are huge; camera might clip. Better battle spawn in central open area around (0, 0) or along main avenue. The central 4 blocks are skipped (|x|<=43 and |z|<=43), leaving a large plaza at center. Spawn player at (0, 55) facing -z, enemy at (0,-55). Camera behind at +z ~250, which is over block at z=129 but high enough maybe. Buildings at z 129 could block view. Better use main avenue x=0? There is a road at z=0 and x=0, and central plaza. Spawn player at z=40, enemy z=-60; camera z=280 still behind block z=129. Could spawn player at z=-40 (south of center) facing +z? Camera behind at z=-280, also buildings. Hmm.

Third-person camera should be above buildings at distance 240; height offset h*0.35 ~40 + pitch*240 ~? pitch 0.18 → y=43+40=83; not above 200m towers. It looks through buildings. Could add camera collision/occlusion or raise camera. For gameplay, we need camera to see monster even among buildings. Typical approach: camera above buildings when close or raise pitch/distance. Starting pitch 0.18 low. Increase to 0.35 and distance maybe 280, y ~96. Still below towers.

We can implement camera obstruction handling: raycast from target to desired camera; if buildings block, pull camera closer or raise. City has boxes; could use raycastBuilding and shorten distance. But if camera is inside a building, pulling closer might still. Better raise camera above obstacle: when desired camera is inside a building footprint, move camera closer until clear. Or make buildings not render when camera inside? We can add camera collision using city.collideCircle at camera x,z; if inside, push out. Also line-of-sight: find first building intersection along target->camera; if hit, place camera before it. But then camera very close and monster fills screen; acceptable.

Simplest: choose spawn on a wide avenue with clear view down the street. Player at (0, 60) facing -z; camera behind at z~300 but road at x=0 means camera x=0 and buildings at x=±43+ not blocking x=0 corridor? Road x=0 runs north-south width 24; camera at x=0 sees down the street, buildings to sides. But blocks at x=±129 etc, not x=0 because central skip? Actually block centers -129,-43,43,129; lots span around 43 with width up to 34, so building at x=43-17=26 to 60; x=0 is clear (road width 24 plus sidewalks). z=129 blocks at x=0? No, no block center x=0. So camera at x=0,z=355 looking down x=0 corridor should see player at z=60; buildings on sides, not center. Screenshot camera x maybe not 0? It is behind player at x=0,z=115 with offset z 240, so camera z=355. Looking at z=115; the central tower in screenshot could be at x=43 side but appears center due to angle? The screenshot's central building maybe x=0? BuildCity skips central (|bx|<=43 && |bz|<=43), but outer low-rise ring at r=245 could be at x near 0,z=245? It places around ring r 245-335; at angle near π/2, x=0,z=245, but condition `if (Math.abs(x) < 220 && Math.abs(z) < 220) continue;` z=245 so not skipped. So a building can sit at x≈0,z≈245 directly between camera (z=355) and player (z=115)! That explains. Also mega towers at (-155,155),(155,-155) etc.

Need camera obstruction avoidance or spawn/camera placement. Better implement camera collision with city boxes: cast ray from target head to desired camera and clamp distance to just before building, and also raise camera. Let's implement in CameraRig.update using game city? CameraRig doesn't have city reference. Pass city into CameraRig constructor or set `cameraRig.city = game.city`. Game creates CameraRig before? It creates city then input then cameraRig. Add `this.cameraRig.city = this.city;`.

In CameraRig.update, after computing desired:
- Determine focus point `focus = target.root.position + (0,h*0.6,0)`.
- Ray from focus to desired; length d.
- `city.raycastBuilding(focus, dir, d)` returns hit point; if hit, set desired = focus + dir * max(30, hit.distance - 8). This puts camera in front of building, closer. But if camera was behind tall building, this will zoom in dramatically; playable. Also if ray starts inside building? focus is monster head, should be clear unless monster inside building (collision prevents).
- Additionally, ensure desired not inside a building footprint at camera y < building height: `collideCircle(desired.x,desired.z, 8)` returns push; if hit and desired.y < hit.height, raise desired.y to hit.height + 20 or move push. Better use raycast first.
- Keep min distance 60.

Need import? CameraRig has THREE and city passed.

Also spawn positions: current battle player at z=115, near block 129. Could set player z=40, enemy z=-50 in central plaza; camera behind at z~280 still may hit ring building at z=245. Raycast will pull in. Good.

Also camera default pitch 0.18 low; raise to 0.3 maybe. In Game.start set input.pitch=0.26. For better view. And zoomTarget 260.

