824:      this.mobileControls.classList.add('visible');

Mobile controls `.visible` added only if coarse pointer. At max-width 760, if we set display:block, it will show even when menu is open (because no `.hidden`). Actually `.mobile-controls` is inside `#ui` and always present, and `.visible` adds display block. If we set display block at max-width, it shows on menu too. We don't want that. Better to add a class based on width or use CSS to only show when HUD is visible. Could use `.hud:not(.hidden) ~ .mobile-controls` but DOM order: HUD is before sandbox-panel and mobile-controls, so sibling selector works. We can do:
```
@media (max-width: 760px) {
  .hud:not(.hidden) ~ .mobile-controls.visible { display: block; }
}
```
But `.visible` is only added on coarse. We can change JS to add visible if coarse OR narrow. At startup, `if (window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches || window.innerWidth <= 760) this.mobileControls.classList.add('visible');` Also handle resize. Then CSS at max-width 760: `.mobile-controls { display: none; }` remains, but `.mobile-controls.visible { display: block; }` already exists globally. Wait, the base `.mobile-controls.visible { display: block; }` is not inside a media query, so it already shows if visible class is added. So simply change JS to add visible on narrow width too. And on resize, update. But if the user resizes from desktop to narrow, visible won't be added unless we listen. Add a function `updateMobileVisibility` called on resize:
```
const mq = window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)');
const apply = () => this.mobileControls.classList.toggle('visible', mq.matches || window.innerWidth <= 760);
mq.addEventListener?.('change', apply); window.addEventListener('resize', apply); apply();
```
But the mobile controls should also hide when HUD hidden (menu). Currently `.visible` shows them regardless of HUD. Does the menu overlay cover them? The menu is a full screen `.screen` with z-index likely above. Let's check z-index. If menu covers, fine. In the mobile menu screenshot, mobile controls were not visible because visible wasn't added. If we add visible on narrow, they might appear over the menu if z-index is lower/higher. Need to check. `.mobile-controls` likely z-index within HUD? It's a sibling after HUD. Let's check CSS z-index.

